<title>UK: SPI Finance sets 125 mln stg perpetual bond.</title>
<headline>SPI Finance sets 125 mln stg perpetual bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SPI FINANCE PLC</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  SCOTTISH PROVIDENT INSTITUTION</p>
<p> AMT    125 MLN STG   COUPON     **	  MATURITY  * PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE   PERPETUAL     ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    13.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.625     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+110 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>	    * CALL AT PAR AFTER 10 YEARS WHEN COUPON STEPS UP.</p>
<p>RESET</p>
<p>		EVERY FIVE YEARS AT HIGHER OF PREVIOUS COUPON OR 210</p>
<p>B.P</p>
<p>		OVER FIVE-YEAR GILT.</p>
<p> MOODY	BAA2	LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A-	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    =	   CRS DEFLT  =	   FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  UK	  TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    =	   SELL CONC  =	   PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.5 PERCENT 2006 GILT</p>
<p> NOTES	SUBORDINATED, EXPECTED RATINGS</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
